# Build output
target/
*.class

# Snapshots written by the app into the project root, e.g.
#   JAVA_OPTS=-Djavaview.snapshot=shot.png ./run.sh
# (the README screenshot under docs/ is tracked on purpose)
/*.png

# The npm package's build output: the templates copied in beside it, and the framework laid out as
# a Maven repository. Both are staged by npm/scripts/build-package.sh and both are carried in the
# published tarball; neither is source, and one of them is a copy of the other templates. The
# sources next to them -- npm/cli.js, npm/src/, npm/package.json, npm/scripts/ -- are tracked.
/npm/templates/
/npm/lib/
/npm/*.tgz

# Editors
.idea/
*.iml
.vscode/
# Editor-tool state (not project content)
.alma-snapshots/

# One agent, one worktree -- kept inside the project rather than beside it, so the app's file tree
# and the editor see it without a second checkout to remember. Ignored because it is a second
# checkout of this same repository, not content.
.worktrees/

# The WebView2 loader DLL: fetched by windows-probe/fetch-loader.ps1 and checksum-verified.
# A third-party binary, like the Tailwind standalone binary — staged, not tracked.
/windows-probe/loader/

# The smoke writes its stage log beside the module; not source.
/windows-probe/smoke-result.txt
/windows-probe/smoke-page.png
